determinants has the same value?\n\n*Hint: Use elementary row operations to make the entries above and below ${a}_{22}$ equal to zero.*" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14058571/state.json" "file_sha256" "8b8c1a36b45ee80b8eae27abfb992b604a32b593eb2ab4e0e1b14d19d24dfd8f"} {"question" "q-42902" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's make entries above and below ${a}_{22}=1$ equal to zero using elementary row operations.\n\nSince adding a multiple of one row (or column) to another row (column) in a matrix does not change the value of its determinant, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & -3 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 3 & 4 & 3 & -2 \\\\ -1 & -1 & -4 & 4\\end{aligned}| &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+2{R}_{2} \\\\ {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-4){R}_{2} \\\\ {R}_{4}:={R}_{4}+{R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ -5 & 0 & -5 & 10 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -2 & 1\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the result along the $2$nd column, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,|\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ -5 & 0 & -5 & 10 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -2 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\cdot (-1)^{2+2}|\\begin{aligned}5 & 1 & -3 \\\\ -5 & -5 & 10 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}5 & 1 & -3 \\\\ -5 & -5 & 10 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 1\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14058571/state.json" "file_sha256" "8b8c1a36b45ee80b8eae27abfb992b604a32b593eb2ab4e0e1b14d19d24dfd8f"} {"question" "q-42902" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14058571/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9a9c5b9d5