e" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14058571/state.json" "file_sha256" "8b8c1a36b45ee80b8eae27abfb992b604a32b593eb2ab4e0e1b14d19d24dfd8f"} {"question" "q-91166" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's make entries below ${a}_{14}=3$ equal to zero using elementary row operations.\n\nSince adding a multiple of one row (or column) to another row (column) in a matrix does not change the value of its determinant, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,|\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 & -3 & 3 \\\\ -3 & -4 & -2 & 12 \\\\ -7 & 2 & 3 & -6 \\\\ 1 & 3 & -2 & -3\\end{aligned}| &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-4){R}_{1} \\\\ {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+2{R}_{1} \\\\ {R}_{4}:={R}_{4}+{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 & -3 & 3 \\\\ -11 & 4 & 10 & 0 \\\\ -3 & -2 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1 & -5 & 0\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the result along the $4$th column, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,|\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 & -3 & 3 \\\\ -11 & 4 & 10 & 0 \\\\ -3 & -2 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1 & -5 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3\\cdot (-1)^{1+4}|\\begin{aligned}-11 & 4 & 10 \\\\ -3 & -2 & -3 \\\\ 3 & 1 & -5\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-3|\\begin{aligned}-11 & 4 & 10 \\\\ -3 & -2 & -3 \\\\ 3 & 1 & -5\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14058571/state.json" "file_sha256" "8b8c1a36b45ee80b8eae27abfb992b604a32b593eb2ab4e0e1b14d19d24dfd8f"} {"question" "q-91166" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14058571/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9a9c5b9d5c6d4071482066f8a11cb4fd6e5ea09b44a5432efa00d710dabfd4fd"} {"question" "q-91166" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/r